Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: wb-echo
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, docker-ce, wb-docker-app
Description: Echo utility service for Wiren Board controllers
 Installs a minimal echo/utility service as a docker-compose service managed by
 wb-docker-app. It exists to prove the "thin per-app package + shared helper"
 model (issue #7): the whole package is the package-owned base
 docker-compose.yml (with the wb.* labels) shipped to
 /usr/lib/wb-docker-app/echo/ plus thin maintainer scripts. The maintainer
 scripts call into the shared helper: postinst runs "wb-docker-app install echo"
 and prerm runs "wb-docker-app remove echo" — no lifecycle logic is duplicated
 here. Installing it reuses the already-provisioned wb network and mosquitto
 listener; it gets its own public port and a distinct internal loopback port,
 so it never collides with Node-RED.
